      "writtenOn": "2014-07-01T09:17:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So since \u0027type\u0027 is part of the hash, I\u0027m not sure how the wrong ID can be removed.  Are you concerned about (once the full cross-backend ID functionality is implemented) that someone could try and pass a public ID representing a group to delete_user()?  If so, this should fail since delete_user() in the manager should:\n\n1) call get_id_mapping() to get the local entity info.  If this is not a user entity, then return UserNotFound.\n\n2) try and call the backend to delete that local entity\n\n3) assuming 1) and 2) worked, it would then delete the mapping\n\nThis seems the right level to be doing this....but open to other views.",
